WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.720
After confirming your shipments in step 2, it's time to print your box labels.

00:00:06.720 --> 00:00:08.160
If you have

00:00:08.160 --> 00:00:13.355
any pallets in your shipment, you'll confirm those details and print carrier labels in the next

00:00:13.355 --> 00:00:13.680
steps.

00:00:14.560 --> 00:00:18.160
If there are no pallets in your shipment, this will be your final step.

00:00:18.880 --> 00:00:23.680
First, you'll want to review the ship from and ship date fields to ensure they are correct.

00:00:24.240 --> 00:00:29.520
You can edit the ship date at this point, but if your ship from field needs to be changed,

00:00:29.520 --> 00:00:32.044
you'll need to go back to step 1.

00:00:32.044 --> 00:00:35.200
Next, review details for each shipment in the shipment card.

00:00:35.760 --> 00:00:38.762
Select rename if you would like to update the shipment name.

00:00:38.762 --> 00:00:40.400
If you want to edit shipment

00:00:40.400 --> 00:00:44.100
contents, select view or edit contents in the shipment card.

00:00:44.100 --> 00:00:46.320
The window that appears lets you

00:00:46.320 --> 00:00:52.105
view box allocation across shipments, print your pack list and edit unit quantities.

00:00:52.105 --> 00:00:53.440
You can adjust

00:00:53.440 --> 00:00:58.692
up to 6 units or 5% of total units, whichever is greater.

00:00:58.692 --> 00:01:00.880
Select validate updates when finished.

00:01:00.880 --> 00:01:06.480
To print box labels, select the drop down menu in each shipment card to choose the size of your

00:01:06.480 --> 00:01:06.933
labels.

00:01:06.933 --> 00:01:10.107
Then select print to generate a PDF.

00:01:10.107 --> 00:01:13.280
If you're using an Amazon partnered carrier,

00:01:13.280 --> 00:01:18.960
your PDF will include an FBA Box ID label as well as a carrier label for each box.

00:01:19.760 --> 00:01:25.760
FBA Box ID labels help us more efficiently manage your shipments once they arrive at an Amazon

00:01:25.760 --> 00:01:26.667
fulfillment center.

00:01:26.667 --> 00:01:32.560
For non-partnered carriers, your PDF will only include FBA Box ID labels.

00:01:33.360 --> 00:01:38.800
You'll need to work with your carrier to create carrier labels, then apply both to each box.

00:01:39.360 --> 00:01:44.444
For pallet shipments, your PDF will also include only FBA Box ID labels.

00:01:44.444 --> 00:01:46.400
Make sure to apply these

00:01:46.400 --> 00:01:52.400
labels to each box so that they will be visible when the pallet is unpacked at our fulfillment center.

00:01:53.200 --> 00:01:58.800
Once all your labels have been applied, your next steps will vary based on your selections in step

00:01:58.800 --> 00:01:59.246
two.

00:01:59.246 --> 00:02:05.040
For small parcel shipments with an Amazon partnered carrier, you've completed the workflow

00:02:05.040 --> 00:02:07.941
and you're ready to hand off your shipment.

00:02:07.941 --> 00:02:09.392
Click view tracking details.

00:02:09.392 --> 00:02:10.480
We'll track your

00:02:10.480 --> 00:02:13.572
shipments and change the status to shipped for you.

00:02:13.572 --> 00:02:16.320
For small parcel shipments with a non-partnered

00:02:16.320 --> 00:02:21.520
carrier, you can also click view tracking details and hand off your shipment to the carrier.

00:02:22.160 --> 00:02:25.316
Then you'll need to provide tracking IDs for your boxes.

00:02:25.316 --> 00:02:27.840
This can be done in the final step

00:02:27.840 --> 00:02:34.165
tracking details that will populate once you complete step three or by navigating to your shipping

00:02:34.165 --> 00:02:34.560
queue

00:02:34.560 --> 00:02:36.571
and clicking track shipment.

00:02:36.571 --> 00:02:41.600
For pallet shipments, select continue to carrier and pallet information

00:02:41.600 --> 00:02:47.360
to proceed to step four.
